    "english_prompt": "Yes\nTranslate the sentence given below into Gujarati.\nOne of the most important benefits of preserving historical buildings and monuments is that\nthey serve as tangible evidence of historical events for future generations.\nછે\nઅૈિતહાિસક ઇમારતાે અને સ્મારકાેની દેખરેખના સાૈથી મહત્ત્વના લાભાે પૈકીનાે અેક લાભ અે કે તે ભાિવ પેઢીઅાે માટે\nઅૈિતહાિસક ઘટનાઅાેનાે અદ્રશ્ય પુરાવાે અાપે છે.\nઅૈિતહાિસક ઇમારતાે અને સ્મારકાેની હયાતીના સાૈથી મહત્ત્વનાે લાભ અે કે તે ભાિવ પેઢીઅાે માટે અૈિતહાિસક પ્રસંગાેનાે નકામાે\nપુરાવાે રજૂ કરે છે.\nઅૈિતહાિસક ઇમારતાે અને યાદાેની સફાઇના સાૈથી મહત્ત્વના લાભાેમાં અેક લાભ અે કે તે ભાિવ લાેકાે માટે અૈિતહાિસક\nઘટનાઅાેની સાિબતી અાપે છે.\nઅૈિતહાિસક ઇમારતાે અને સ્મારકાેની જાળવણીના સાૈથી મહત્ત્વના લાભાે પૈકીનાે અેક લાભ અે કે તે ભાિવ પેઢીઅાે માટે\nઅૈિતહાિસક ઘટનાઅાેનાે નક્કર પુરાવાે રજૂ કરે છે\nSub-Section Number : 2\nSub-Section Id : 63068045803\nQuestion Shuffling Allowed : Yes\nQuestion Id : 630680743092 Question Type : COMPREHENSION Sub Question Shuffling\nAllowed : Yes Group Comprehension Questions : No Question Pattern Type : NonMatrix\nQuestion Numbers : (82 to 85)\nRead the passage given below and answer the questions\nEvery individual is a member of a specific culture that shapes their worldview, opinions,\nbehaviors, and daily activities. With the advent of technological advancements and traveling,\npeople now have the possibility to interact with others from all around the world and enrich\ntheir knowledge. It is therefore crucial to understand the concept of culture better to prevent\ncultural misunderstandings and conflicts.\nTo understand culture, it is essential to define what it is. Culture refers to the characteristics\nand knowledge of a particular group of people, encompassing language, religion, cuisine,\nsocial habits, music, and arts. However, the definition goes much further by considering the\ndistinguishing features of specific nationalities, behavioral patterns and interactions,\nsocialization, and cognitive constructs. Since every culture is unique, it is essential to\nunderstand the differences that exist. Most of the cultural differences can be observed in the\nspecificities of communication. For example, highly people-oriented cultures are usually open\nand easy-going, where individuals are more likely to remain in close proximity, engage in deep\nconversations, and maintain eye contact. In contrast, cultures that value privacy and intimacy\ntend to perceive such behavior as inappropriate. Such cultural differences often lead to\nmisunderstandings, which can prevent people from developing meaningful relationships.\nTherefore, it is crucial to educate oneself and adapt behavior to engage in respectful and\nappropriate communication with those from different cultures.\nIn conclusion, culture is a complex subject that requires thorough research. As individuals\ntravel around the world, meet new people, and establish personal relationships, it is essential\nto educate oneself about cultural differences that can lead to misunderstandings. Learning\nmore about them and training oneself to adapt can not only save time but also contribute to\nthe creation of meaningful friendships with people from different cultures. Effective cross-\ncultural communication is essential in a globalized world, and understanding culture is the first\nstep to achieving it.\nSub questions",
